    "body": "## Problem\n\nWe could replace non-interactive ex-mode (`nvim -es/-Es`) with a Lua script.\n\nBenefits:\n\n- Allows deleting lots of globals and special-cases.\n- Unifies \"script mode\" internals (`nvim -l/-es`).\n\nRelated:\n\n- https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/40962\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nReplace *non-interactive* Ex-mode with a small Lua script, as follows:\n\n\n    main.c parses -es/-Es (!input_istext)\n      - don't set exmode_active / don't input_start()\n        - fd 0 stays free and Lua can read Ex commands from io.lines().\n      - set `headless` + `silent`, delegate to `vim._core.exmode`\n    vim._core.exmode:\n      for line in io.lines() do\n        local ok, res = pcall(vim.api.nvim_exec2, line, { output = true })\n        io.write(res.output or '')   -- explicit stdout, no msg-routing.\n      end\n      os.exit(code)\n\nThe core logic is shared by [interactive](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/40962) + non-interactive Ex-mode: \"Ex line runner\" that does execute + optional auto-print.\n\n## Eliminate\n\nThis allows us to drop:\n\n```\nex_no_reprint\nex_pressedreturn (also eliminates save/restore boilerplate from eval.c and autocmd.c)\npending_exmode_active\nexmode_plus\ndo_exmode()\n```\n\nSee also https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/40962\n\n\n\n\n",
